-extends "channels/channel_claim_form.html"
-load i18n compress temba

-block pre-form
  -blocktrans trimmed with name=brand.name
    You can connect a <a href="https://developers.line.me/messaging-api/overview">LINE bot</a> to your {{ name }}
    workspace to automate sending and receiving LINE messages.
  -blocktrans trimmed
    To start creating a LINE bot, go to <a href="https://developers.line.me/messaging-api/getting-started">Getting started with the Messaging API</a>.

  %ol.steps.card
    %li
      -blocktrans trimmed
        Go to the <a href="https://developers.line.me/channels/">LINE Channels</a> page and add a new channel.

    %li
      -blocktrans trimmed
        Create a LINE account using the app on your smartphone.

    %li
      -blocktrans trimmed
        Enable login via web application in <i>Settings</i> &gt; <i>Account</i> &gt; <i>Allow login</i>.

    %li
      -blocktrans trimmed
        Register your email and password in <i>Settings</i> &gt; <i>Account</i> &gt; <i>Email Account</i>.

    %li
      -blocktrans trimmed
        Create a new LINE business account with Messaging API enabled.

      %ol
        %li
          -blocktrans trimmed
            In <a href="https://business.line.me/en/">LINE Business Center</a>, select <i>Messaging API</i> under
            <i>Services</i>.

        %li
          -blocktrans trimmed
            Select <i>Start using Messaging API</i>.

        %li
          -blocktrans trimmed
            Enter your credentials and wait for the confirmation code in the app.

          .important
            %p
              -blocktrans trimmed
                Note: You'll need to create a LINE business account. Some information will be requested, such as
                address and phone number.

        %li
          -blocktrans trimmed
            After creating your LINE business account, you'll see the page to add a new <i>Messaging API</i> channel.
            Enter the name, select the appropriate category, and click OK.

        %li
          -blocktrans trimmed
            Next, click <i>LINE @ Manager</i> to be redirected to the API activation page.

        %li
          -blocktrans trimmed
            Click "Enable API" and confirm. Your API status will change to <i>Valid</i>.

        %li
          -blocktrans trimmed
            Enable webhooks and click <i>Save</i>.

    %li
      -blocktrans trimmed
        Set your bot:

      %ol
        %li
          -blocktrans trimmed
            Click the "Accounts" menu at the top of the page at
            <a href="https://business.line.me">https://business.line.me</a>.

        %li
          -blocktrans trimmed
            In your chosen channel, click the <i>LINE Developers</i> button, accept the terms, and you'll be directed
            to a page with the information needed for the form below (channel ID, channel name, channel secret, and
            channel access token).

          %p
            -blocktrans trimmed
              Note: To generate the channel access token, click the <i>Issue</i> button.

-block extra-style
  {{ block.super }}

  :css
    .info {
      width: 800px;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    .form-group {
      margin-bottom:15px;
    }

    #id_* {
      width: 340px;
    }
